# The Slums' signage (src/models/props/signage.gd): a hand-painted mural
# half-covered by a hoarding that is still cheerfully selling something, and the
# light a billboard throws on the wet street under it.
#
# tools/tour.sh tours/slums-signage.tour --seed=3 --place=coast --hour=23 --weather=rain:0.85 --put=mural,billboard
#
# STAGED ON THE COAST ON PURPOSE, and this is the one thing to know before
# reading the frames: the Slums' own landscape file belongs to another builder
# (slums/dome) and does not exist on this branch, so there is no Slums to stand
# in. What is proved here is the SIGNAGE half -- that the models stand up, that a
# billboard is a real LIGHT and not only a glowing face, and that its light
# reaches the ground a player is walking on. When the landscape lands this tour
# should lose `--put` and say `place slums`, and the rain should come off, since
# the Slums is wet at every hour without it.
#
# The rain is here because `neon_wetness` takes max(BiomeDef.wet, settled rain)
# and the coast declares 0.15. It is standing in for the Slums' own permanent
# wet, which is `dome`'s to set.

# No `at prop:` here, deliberately. `--put` already stands the player in front of
# what it set out, and `at prop:mural` cannot find a footing beside a wall whose
# solid radius is 1.5 -- it refused with "nothing stands beside the mural". The
# walk backwards is what a player would do to see the top of it.
wait 0.8
walk 0,-1 0.9
wait 0.5
shot 01-mural-under-the-hoarding with prop:mural

# Further back, so the frame holds the GROUND the hoarding is lighting as well as
# the hoarding. That is the claim worth making: paint emits nothing and a
# projection lights the street, and both are in this one picture.
walk 0,-1 0.8
wait 0.6
# The floor is MEASURED, not reasoned: this frame came back with 22120 pixels of
# the billboard's own white, so 8000 leaves room for the walk landing a little
# short under load while still failing if the face dims by three times. It has to
# be a real floor, because the bug it guards against is one that already
# happened -- the panel burning on its own face while `15_lights.source_lit`
# quietly said it was not a light at all, and nothing anywhere raised a word.
shot 02-the-hoardings-light-on-the-ground with prop:mural,pixels:F2E8D2:8000

walk 1,0 1.0
wait 0.6
shot 03-billboard-over-the-street with prop:billboard

# And at noon. A billboard is the one light in this game that is never switched
# off (15_lights `source_lit`), because nobody living under it decides -- so the
# frame that proves it is a clear midday one.
hour 12
weather clear:0
wait 0.8
shot 04-still-selling-at-noon with prop:billboard
